        {
          "id": "danebank2021-y12e1-mc9",
          "type": "mc",
          "stem": "A particle is initially positioned at \\(x=-2\\). Its motion has velocity of \\(v=\\dfrac{1}{t+e}\\). Which of the following will be true when the particle reaches the origin?",
          "difficulty": "hard",
          "options": [
            "\\(t=2,\\ v=\\dfrac{1}{2+e}\\)",
            "\\(t=e,\\ \\dot{x}=\\dfrac{1}{2e}\\)",
            "\\(t=e^2,\\ v=\\dfrac{1}{e^2+e}\\)",
            "\\(t=e^3-e,\\ v=e^{-3}\\)"
          ],
          "answer": 3,
          "hint": "Integrate the velocity to get \\(x\\), use \\(x(0)=-2\\) for the constant, then find when \\(x=0\\).",
          "steps": [
            {
              "explain": "Integrate.",
              "work": "\\(x=\\int\\dfrac{1}{t+e}dt=\\ln(t+e)+C\\)"
            },
            {
              "explain": "At \\(t=0\\), \\(x=-2\\).",
              "work": "\\(-2=\\ln e+C=1+C\\ \\Rightarrow\\ C=-3\\), so \\(x=\\ln(t+e)-3\\)"
            },
            {
              "explain": "The origin: \\(x=0\\).",
              "work": "\\(\\ln(t+e)=3\\ \\Rightarrow\\ t+e=e^3\\ \\Rightarrow\\ t=e^3-e\\)"
            },
            {
              "explain": "Velocity then.",
              "work": "\\(v=\\dfrac{1}{t+e}=\\dfrac{1}{e^3}=e^{-3}\\) → <span style=\"color:#047857;font-weight:700\">D</span>"
            }
          ],
          "keyPoints": [
            {
              "text": "reaches the origin",
              "note": "Integrate with \\(x(0)=-2\\), then set \\(x=0\\)."
            }
          ],
          "timeLimit": 60,
          "xp": 1,
          "meta": {
            "source": "Danebank School 2021 Trial HSC Examination Mathematics Extension 1",
            "school": "Danebank School",
            "grade": "12",
            "origin": "teacher"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "glenwood2020-pre-q8d",
          "type": "mc",
          "stem": "A particle is moving in a straight line, so that its displacement \\(x\\) metres from a fixed point on the line at \\(t\\) seconds (\\(t>0\\)) is given by \\(x=3t^{3}-t^{2}-2t\\). Find when the acceleration is positive.",
          "difficulty": "medium",
          "options": [
            "\\(t>\\dfrac{1}{9}\\)",
            "\\(t>\\dfrac{1}{9}\\) seconds and \\(t<0\\)",
            "\\(0<t<\\dfrac{1}{9}\\)",
            "\\(t>1\\)"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "hint": "Differentiate once for VELOCITY \\(v=\\dfrac{dx}{dt}\\), again for ACCELERATION \\(a=\\dfrac{d^{2}x}{dt^{2}}\\). Then solve \\(a>0\\) for \\(t\\) (remember \\(t>0\\)).",
          "steps": [
            {
              "explain": "Velocity: differentiate \\(x=3t^{3}-t^{2}-2t\\).",
              "work": "\\(v=\\dfrac{dx}{dt}=9t^{2}-2t-2\\)"
            },
            {
              "explain": "Acceleration: differentiate \\(v\\).",
              "work": "\\(a=\\dfrac{dv}{dt}=18t-2\\)"
            },
            {
              "explain": "Solve \\(a>0\\): \\(18t-2>0\\Rightarrow t>\\dfrac{2}{18}=\\dfrac{1}{9}\\).",
              "work": "\\(18t-2>0\\ \\Rightarrow\\ t>\\dfrac{1}{9}\\)"
            },
            {
              "explain": "Check with the condition \\(t>0\\): \\(t>\\dfrac{1}{9}\\) is already positive. The acceleration is positive for \\(t>\\dfrac{1}{9}\\) seconds (about 0.11 s).",
              "work": "\\(t>\\dfrac{1}{9}\\ \\text{seconds}\\)"
            },
            {
              "explain": "Why not the others: B includes \\(t<0\\), which is excluded; C is the interval where \\(a<0\\); D comes from \\(a=0\\) with an arithmetic slip.",
              "work": ""
            },
            {
              "explain": "So the correct choice is option <span style=\"color:#047857;font-weight:700\">A</span>.",
              "work": ""
            }
          ],
          "keyPoints": [
            {
              "text": "Find when the acceleration is positive.",
              "note": "\\(a=\\dfrac{d^2x}{dt^2}=18t-2>0\\)"
            }
          ],
